  "question": {
    "text": "Two common tangents to the circle $x^2+y^2=2 a^2$ and parabola $y^2=8 a x$ are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1IpcD",
      "text": "\n$x=\\pm(y+2 a)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RhVp9",
      "text": "\n$y=\\pm(x+2 a)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "7vGYC",
      "text": "\n$x=\\pm(y+a)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OV8WF",
      "text": "\n$y=\\pm(x+a)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Any tangent to the parabola $y^2=8 a x$ is\n$$\ny=m x+\\frac{2 a}{m} \n$$\nIf (i) is a tangent to the circle, $x^2+y^2=2 a^2$ then, $\\quad \\sqrt{2} a=\\pm \\frac{2 a}{m \\sqrt{m^2+1}}$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow m^2\\left(1+m^2\\right)=2 \\Rightarrow\\left(m^2+2\\right)\\left(m^2-1\\right)=0 ; \\Rightarrow m=\\pm 1\n$$\nSo, $y=\\pm(x+2 a)$",
    "image": null
  },
